WEBVTT

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:14.780
<i>In the year 2020 C.E.,</i>

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:18.280
<i>the human world is connected by a network.</i>

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:24.160
<i>Inhabiting it is
an unknown life form called Digimon.</i>

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:48.230
<i>Oh Yeah!
Be strong, jump on, become the wind</i>

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:48.230
<i>Oh Yeah!
tsuyogatte tobinotte kaze ni natte</i>

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:54.320
<i>Pass the orbit beyond the sky</i>

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:54.320
<i>oozora kidou wo koero</i>

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:11.090
<i>Can't hold back this rushing speed</i>

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:11.090
<i>osaekirenai maenomeri na speed</i>

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>A familiar town turns into a diorama</i>

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>minareta machi ga diorama ni naru</i>

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:21.310
<i>Burst through the unclear skies</i>

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:21.310
<i>futoumei na sora tsukinukerunda</i>

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:26.480
<i>Blow away your worries and discontent</i>

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:26.480
<i>nayami toka fuman toka futtobashite</i>

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:31.900
<i>Who needs a journey that's by the book</i>

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:31.900
<i>manual doori no tabi nanka irane</i>

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:37.700
<i>Even if you're lost or trembling,
Raise the altitude</i>

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:37.700
<i>mayottemo furuetemo koudo agete</i>

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:42.580
<i>Oh Yeah!
Show off, mess up, stand back up</i>

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:42.580
<i>Oh Yeah!
ikigatte shikujitte tachiagatte</i>

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:47.790
<i>The unknown horizon I watch with you</i>

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:47.790
<i>kimi to mitsumeru michi naru chiheisen</i>

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.670
<i>Now, be strong, jump on, become the wind</i>

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.670
<i>saa tsuyogatte tobinotte kaze ni natte</i>

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:58.470
<i>Use the sun
That lights tomorrow as a guide</i>

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:58.470
<i>asu wo terasu taiyou
mejirushi ni shitesa</i>

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:04.310
<i>Fly off to the Glorious World of freedom</i>

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:04.310
<i>tonde ike jiyuu na Glorious World</i>

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:08.770
<i>Taichi and his friends now know</i>

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:12.360
<i>the Holy Digimon is the key
to saving Tokyo.</i>

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:16.240
<i>As the group wandered the forest,</i>

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:22.240
<i>they met Mimi Tachikawa, a human girl
who ran a small kingdom with Tanemon,</i>

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:24.990
<i>and her friend, Palmon.</i>

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:29.870
<i>In the shadows of the battle
with Tuskmon who ransacked the orchard,</i>

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:33.090
<i>Mimi was attacked by a cunning enemy.</i>

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:41.340
<i>That was when Mimi's Digivice lit up
and Palmon evolved into Togemon.</i>

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:46.770
<i>With Mimi in their party,</i>

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:51.020
<i>Taichi and his friends head for the sea
to cross over to the continent.</i>

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:02.530
You sure have improved, Palmon!

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.700
It's as tasty as the real Golden Tippy!

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:11.540
This sure is great tea!

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:13.460
The snacks are yummy too!

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:15.040
Uh-huh!

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:18.510
Seriously, what a peaceful moment...

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:21.800
Wait, should we be taking our time
having tea like this?

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:27.180
My grandpa told me
that traders who rush make less money.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:32.310
Palmon, how much further
is the sea from here?

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.310
It's right there.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:35.440
What?

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:49.330
It's the sea!

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:01.170
THAT BOY IS JOE KIDO

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.970
Do you see the continent?

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:07.470
I can't see anything yet.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:11.930
Birdramon, aren't we heavy?

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.350
I'm fine!

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:18.110
I just hope it's a distance
I can fly across...

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:31.450
What's that?

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:32.870
What's wrong?

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.080
That!

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:41.380
Huh?

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:46.590
Watch out!

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:54.180
Sora!

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.820
Sora! Agumon!

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:07.780
Taichi!

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:09.780
Taichi! Agumon!

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:12.290
Sora! I'm glad you're okay!

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:14.080
Birdramon?

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:16.290
Piyomon!

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:19.790
Swim!

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:26.260
Marching Fishes!

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:30.760
Fish?!

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:33.180
Follow me!

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.320
We're saved...

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:48.410
Piyomon, are you okay?

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:51.330
Yes, I'm glad you're okay too.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:53.450
What happened?

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:55.450
We don't really know.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.710
Something squiggly
came out of a whirlpool.

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:01.130
That's Gesomon.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:02.880
Gesomon?

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:06.470
It's a vicious Digimon who dwells
at the bottom of the sea.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.220
GOMAMON

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:10.720
When anyone tries to cross the strait,
Gesomon attacks like that.

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:12.720
And you are?

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.720
I'm Gomamon!

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:16.930
So you're the one who saved us!

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:20.350
Thank you. You have some amazing powers!

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:24.230
Marching Fishes!
It's my special technique!

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:27.240
You guys must be the Chosen Ones.

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:30.030
You know about us?!

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:33.240
Yeah, because I have a partner too.

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:34.490
A partner...

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:36.000
Oh! A human?!

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:39.500
That means another child
who'll find the Holy Digimon with us.

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:42.500
Well, supposedly...

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:58.020
<i>There are no signs of power
returning to the city yet.</i>

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:04.520
MYSTERIOUS POWER OUTAGE SPREADS

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:04.520
<i>The power outage has spread to parts of
Kanagawa, Chiba and Saitama.</i>

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:08.190
<i>In Kawaguchi-shi, Saitama-shi,
and Urayasu-shi,</i>

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.990
<i>the power supply has shut off since 7 a.m.</i>

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:17.540
Oh, the microwave stopped!

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:20.210
CHAOS CONTINUES
WITHIN METROPOLITAN AREA

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:20.210
What a problem...

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:25.000
<i>Experts say that
if there's a delay in recovery,</i>

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:30.090
<i>there's a fear that the city of Tokyo
will cease to operate in a few days...</i>

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:33.800
Ugh, things are becoming worse and worse.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:38.810
We must hurry and join Taichi-san's group!

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:45.690
MIDDLE SCHOOL ENTRANCE EXAMS

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:56.910
What is this guy doing?

00:07:57.530 --> 00:07:58.490
Studying?

00:07:58.620 --> 00:07:59.700
Here?!

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:05.040
Joe, I've brought over
the other Chosen Ones.

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:07.960
Hm?

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:12.300
Humans?!

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:15.010
I'm Taichi Yagami.

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:17.140
I'm Sora Takenouchi.

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:19.600
Mimi Tachikawa, a fourth-grader.

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:21.680
I'm Agumon!

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:22.640
Piyomon!

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.020
Palmon here.

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:26.230
Oh?

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:28.980
So there's no grown-ups...

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:30.320
Huh?

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:34.320
Tell me! How can I get back
to the other world?!

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:37.740
How? Beats me...

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:42.500
Anyhow, we need your help.

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:43.790
Huh?

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:48.630
At this rate,
Tokyo will be in big trouble...

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:52.970
And that problem is caused
by this Digital World.

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:56.840
So, they say we need to go and stop that.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:58.680
We?

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:01.720
Let's go find the Holy Digimon together!

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:04.640
We need you and Gomamon's help!

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:12.150
Oh, I'm Joe Kido,
a sixth-grader at Musako Elementary.

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:13.110
What?

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:16.030
That means he's our senpai!

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:20.160
Oh, come to think of it, I might've
seen him at our recent camping trip...

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:24.660
I still can't believe a story like that.

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:28.920
Save Tokyo from a crisis? Why me?

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:33.050
I have important entrance exams
next year and I have no time!

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:38.840
Whoever controls summer,
controls the exams!

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:41.890
But why am I the only one
in a place like this?!

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:47.310
While I'm stuck here,
my rivals are all getting ahead!

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:52.070
My family is a line of doctors,

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:55.780
and I must become one myself
in the future!

00:09:55.900 --> 00:10:00.320
If you want me to contribute to society,
I'll do it all when I grow up!

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:05.120
But right now, I have to study!

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:15.800
Are we really taking this guy with us?

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:21.760
Let's go!

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:27.390
Joe, you came to this world and met me,
because you have an important role!

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:29.900
We're partn--

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:31.940
You've been a great help.

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:35.400
I do appreciate it,

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:39.360
but... I don't ever remember
becoming partners.

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:46.700
Hey, Senpai.

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:50.120
I know it's dangerous,
and we can't force you to come,

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:53.380
but we're the only ones that can do this.

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:59.430
Let's say that just us kids travel
around this bizarre and dangerous world,

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:02.760
and we struggle
to accomplish that so-called goal.

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:06.520
Is there any guarantee that we'll be able
to return to our world?

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:08.770
Joe...

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:12.020
Gomamon, you can go with them.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:15.070
I'm going to stay here and study.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:27.200
As long as Gesomon's there,
we can't cross this strait.

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:29.910
We have to chase Gesomon away somehow.

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:31.670
But how?

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:32.920
What?

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:53.560
Are you really not going with everybody?

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:57.150
Even if I did,
there'd be nothing I could do.

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:02.780
Then I should just stay here
and do what I need to do.

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:20.420
Piyomon, you should stay
and rest for a while.

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:23.180
Let's team up with Agumon and Palmon.

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:27.550
We have no chance in the ocean,
but if we're on land...

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:29.930
We'll draw Gesomon out here!

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:33.690
Okay, then victory will be ours!

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:36.110
We'll fight for Piyomon too!

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:38.360
Leave it to us!

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:40.690
Agumon... Palmon...

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:46.200
If that's the plan,
I'll be the bait to draw Gesomon over.

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:47.620
Gomamon?!

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:53.830
I'll use my Marching Fishes
to taunt and lure Gesomon over here.

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:56.830
Gomamon, what about Joe Senpai?

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:03.630
Joe... has too much on his mind
with stuff he has to do

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:06.890
and has no room for anything else.

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:10.850
And now that he's got
even more things to do,

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:13.640
he's perplexed and struggling.

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:17.060
Even if he looks
like he's absorbed in studying.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:23.110
But one day, he'll become a great human
that'll help everyone out!

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:29.120
That's why I'm gonna help everyone out
for Joe right now!

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:36.580
Here we go! Marching Fishes!

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:47.260
Here it comes!

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:54.060
Come, Gesomon! Over here!

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:07.910
C'mon, over here!
If you want me, come and get me!

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:25.210
I see the whirlpool!

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:28.050
Good, they're coming this way!

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:30.680
Gomamon, keep it up!

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:39.060
Gomamon...

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:44.320
Just a little further...

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:50.950
Gomamon!

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:56.700
Gomamon!

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:00.250
Are you okay?!

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:02.170
Hang in there!

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:04.750
Joe...

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:06.130
Joe Senpai!

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:09.510
Hurry and get away from there!
Take Gomamon with you!

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:21.810
GESOMON

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:29.280
That's Gesomon?!

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:31.610
We only saw the tentacles earlier.

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:33.530
But now, the whole thing is here!

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:34.580
Agumon!

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:36.290
You're on, Palmon!

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:37.370
Yeah!

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:46.300
Agumon Evolution!

00:15:57.470 --> 00:15:59.350
Greymon!

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:04.310
Palmon Evolution!

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:09.070
Togemon!

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:26.040
Gomamon...
why did you do something so reckless?

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:29.340
I was... waiting for a long time...

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:30.460
What?

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:40.850
Prickly Bang-Bang!

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:52.240
Togemon!

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:05.670
I was looking forward to it,

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:10.130
always wondering what kind
of human my partner would be.

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:13.420
That's why when I finally met you, Joe...

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:16.010
I was really happy.

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:34.650
Weren't you disappointed?

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:37.870
To find out you were waiting
for a human like me?

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:39.620
No, that's not true!

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:40.530
Gomamon?

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:43.250
That's not true at all...

00:17:57.630 --> 00:18:03.390
I was waiting
for no one else but you, Joe.

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:08.270
I think so myself, so there's no mistake!

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:27.370
Gomamon, are you okay?

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:29.830
What you need to do in this world

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:33.920
is not something you need to get done
by yourself, Joe.

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:38.130
You have others like Taichi,
and you have me too.

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:40.180
We'll do it together!

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:42.140
So don't worry!

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:50.480
You're right, Gomamon.

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:54.900
I wasn't alone, because you were there
for me in this world.

00:18:55.190 --> 00:18:56.490
If I were by myself,

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:59.490
I probably wouldn't have been able
to even study.

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:00.910
Gomamon,

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:02.620
you're my...

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:06.870
I'm your partner!

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:12.630
Uh?

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:17.630
Gomamon Evolution!

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:32.600
That's...

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:38.740
IKKAKUMON

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:38.440
Ikkakumon!

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:42.240
Ikkakumon...

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:51.960
Ikkakumon!

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:10.140
You're not getting away!

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:12.650
Harpoon Vulcan!

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:28.660
Togemon!

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:30.250
Coconut...

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:31.790
Punch!

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:35.290
Greymon!

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:43.050
I'll finish you!

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:45.300
Harpoon Vulcan!

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:09.830
Joe Senpai!

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:11.370
That Digimon's strong!

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:14.830
Yeah, since Ikkakumon's my partner.

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:22.210
All right!

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:24.720
Now that I'm coming along,

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:27.510
let's find this so-called
Holy Digimon fast!

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:30.640
Senpai, you're up for it all of a sudden.

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:33.350
I don't have much time!

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:36.600
Whoever controls summer,
controls the exams!

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:40.440
Going forward,
please listen to the me, the olde...

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:42.030
Eh... Eh...

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:44.320
E-E-E-Ehh?!

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:45.450
He flopped!

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:47.160
He really flopped!

00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:49.200
Senpai's flopped!

00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:51.160
He's flopped!

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:57.170
Don't say I flopped!
I'm studying for entrance exams!

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:07.380
<i>As if rolling out of control,
I ran frantically</i>

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:07.380
<i>korogaru youni gamushara ni hashitta</i>

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:11.260
<i>"What's waiting ahead?"</i>

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:11.260
<i>nani ga matteru no?</i>

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:17.770
<i>The headwinds told me</i>

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:17.770
<i>mukaikaze ga oshiete kuretanda</i>

00:22:17.900 --> 00:22:21.320
<i>"Just believe and move forward"</i>

00:22:17.900 --> 00:22:21.320
<i>shinjite susume</i>

00:22:21.770 --> 00:22:24.490
<i>The bitter taste of defeat is a seed</i>

00:22:21.770 --> 00:22:24.490
<i>yaburete shitta kuyashisa wa tane</i>

00:22:24.610 --> 00:22:27.110
<i>It will eventually sprout
And become your wings</i>

00:22:24.610 --> 00:22:27.110
<i>yagate mebuki hane to naru</i>

00:22:27.240 --> 00:22:30.950
<i>I knock on those doors</i>

00:22:27.240 --> 00:22:30.950
<i>sono tobira tataku riyuu</i>

00:22:31.080 --> 00:22:36.790
<i>Because the present shapes the future</i>

00:22:31.080 --> 00:22:36.790
<i>ima ga mirai wo tsukuru kara</i>

00:22:36.910 --> 00:22:39.080
<i>If you want to find a rainbow</i>

00:22:36.910 --> 00:22:39.080
<i>niji wo mitsuketai nara</i>

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:42.250
<i>You must lift your face</i>

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:42.250
<i>kao wo agenakuchatte</i>

00:22:42.380 --> 00:22:47.510
<i>The hands that reached out to us
Make us much stronger</i>

00:22:42.380 --> 00:22:47.510
<i>sashidasareta te ga
bokura wo zutto tsuyoku suru</i>

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:49.590
<i>If you want to catch your dreams</i>

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:49.590
<i>yume wo tsukamitai nara</i>

00:22:49.760 --> 00:22:52.890
<i>Though the step forward is unsteady</i>

00:22:49.760 --> 00:22:52.890
<i>furueru sono ippo mae ni</i>

00:22:53.010 --> 00:22:55.640
<i>Try and take it</i>

00:22:53.010 --> 00:22:55.640
<i>fumi dashite goran yo</i>

00:22:55.770 --> 00:23:00.650
<i>Because you can surely fly now</i>

00:22:55.770 --> 00:23:00.650
<i>ima nara kitto sora mo toberu kara</i>

00:23:01.480 --> 00:23:03.270
<i>Yamato appears once again.</i>

00:23:03.440 --> 00:23:06.900
<i>The six Chosen Ones have finally gathered</i>

00:23:07.030 --> 00:23:08.820
<i>and carry out their shocking plan!</i>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:12.620
<i>Next time on Digimon Adventure:
"The Children's Attack on the Fortress"</i>

00:23:12.740 --> 00:23:15.290
<i>The adventure continues to a new world.</i>
